# Weekend Countdown
// How long until the weekend:  days, hours, minutes and seconds, ticking down every second.

weekend countdown is an app
	its "time" is a date
		// This moment:  set again every second, so the countdown redraws
	every second
		set its time to now
	it "is the weekend" if its time is a weekend day
		// Saturday and Sunday in most places:  the person's region says
	its "time left" is the next weekend - its time
		// A duration:  2 days, 3 hours, 4 minutes and 5 seconds

	to draw it
		// The days, hours, minutes and seconds left, side by side;  on the weekend, a cheer instead
		<container width="32em">
			<segment padding="lg">
				<if it is the weekend>
					<header>It's the weekend!</header>
				<else>
					<text color="grey">Weekend starts in</text>
					<statistics equal size="small">
						<statistic value={the days of its time left} label="Days" />
						<statistic value={the hours of its time left as two digits} label="Hr" />
						<statistic value={the minutes of its time left as two digits} label="Min" />
						<statistic value={the seconds of its time left as two digits} label="Sec" />
					</statistics>
				</if>
			</segment>
		</container>
